# Resource Estimation for Quantum Variational Simulations of the Hubbard Model

**Author:** Zhenyu Cai (Oxford / Quantum Motion)
**arXiv:** 1910.02719 (v4, 1 July 2020)

## Abstract (paraphrased)

We estimate the near-term hardware resources required to run a Hamiltonian
Variational Ansatz (HVA) VQE on the 2D Fermi--Hubbard model. Under a
Jordan--Wigner encoding, a $V$-site spinful Hubbard model uses $N=2V$ qubits.
For the headline case $V=25$ (5$\times$5 lattice, 50 qubits), each HVA block
requires approximately $N_{1q}\approx 650$ single-qubit and
$N_{2q}\approx 1000$ two-qubit gates, giving $\sim 20{,}000$ two-qubit gates
for a full ansatz. A two-qubit gate error rate $p_{2q}\lesssim 10^{-4}$ is
required to keep the mean per-shot error $\mu\lesssim 1$ (with
symmetry-verification mitigation), and each circuit run takes $\sim 250\,\mu s$.

## Key formulas (Appendix A2)

Per-block gate counts as a function of the number of sites $V$:

- $N_{1q}(V) = 4\,V^{3/2} + 7\,V - 4\,\sqrt{V}$
- $N_{2q}(V) = 8\,V^{3/2} + V - 4\,\sqrt{V}$
- $T(V) = (8\sqrt{V} + 5)\,\tau_{1q} + (16\sqrt{V} + 2)\,\tau_{2q}$

Qubit count under Jordan--Wigner:

- $N_{\mathrm{qubits}} = 2\,V$

## Headline point evaluation ($V=25$)

| Quantity      | Paper (stated)                     | Direct evaluation                  |
|---------------|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|
| $N_{1q}$      | $\approx 650$                      | $655$                              |
| $N_{2q}$      | $\approx 1000$                     | $1005$                             |
| $T$           | $\approx 45\tau_{1q}+80\tau_{2q}$  | $45\tau_{1q}+82\tau_{2q}$          |
| $N_{\mathrm{qubits}}$ | $50$                       | $50$ (measured on 2$\times$2, 2$\times$3 substructures) |

## Error-budget arithmetic (Eq.\ 3 paraphrase)

Mean per-shot error at $V=25$, given approximately 26{,}000 two-qubit gates
per ansatz and $p_{2q}=10^{-4}$:

- $\mu \approx 26{,}000 \times 10^{-4} \approx 2.6$ (paper: "$\sim 2.5$").

## Structure

- **Sec 1--2:** Introduction and Hamiltonian setup (single-band Hubbard,
  Jordan--Wigner mapping).
- **Sec 3:** HVA circuit and its expressibility (block structure
  $\exp(-i\theta_v H_v)\exp(-i\theta_h H_h)\exp(-i\theta_U H_U)$).
- **Sec 4:** Resource analysis on silicon spin qubits vs.\ superconducting
  qubits (hardware timing tables).
- **Sec 5:** Symmetry-verification mitigation and its effect on the
  error budget.
- **Appendix A1:** Kivlichan et al.\ fermionic-swap-network construction.
- **Appendix A2:** Primitive-level gate decomposition on silicon-native gates
  and derivation of the closed-form $N_{1q}(V)$, $N_{2q}(V)$, $T(V)$.

## Scope / not tested (in this replication)

- Full 50-qubit ansatz (classically infeasible; paper acknowledges this).
- Hardware-specific $\tau_{1q}$, $\tau_{2q}$ values for silicon vs.
  superconducting qubits.
- Symmetry-verification-mitigation overhead constants.

